  "system": {
    "slug": "cerberus-technician",
    "details": {
      "level": {
        "value": 3
      },
      "publicNotes": "<p>Cerberus Technicians maintain Cerberus equipment, mechs, and ship systems. They carry an omni-tool for remote access and repairs, and can be found in Cerberus facilities and aboard vessels. While not front-line combatants, they can interface with and reactivate disabled mechs or unlock security systems. In desperation they fight with omni-tools and light pistols.</p><p><strong>Reactivate Mech (2 actions):</strong> The Technician remotely reactivates a destroyed LOKI Mech within 30 feet, restoring it to 10 HP with its maximum actions. 1/encounter.</p><p><strong>Override Terminal (3 actions):</strong> The Technician spends a full turn accessing a terminal or security system within 10 feet. On a Computers check (DC 20), they can unlock doors, disable turrets, or access information.</p>",
      "privateNotes": "",
      "publication": {
        "title": "Mass Effect Compendium",
        "authors": "nscarpinatodev",
